Subject: [PATCH] dsd: skip the padding byte of odd DSDIFF chunks

DSDIFF 1.5 section 2.3 requires a padding byte after an odd-sized
chunk body. The chunk's declared size excludes both the 12-byte header
and that padding byte. Skipping only len + 12 leaves the pad in front of
the next chunk ID; for example a valid 19-byte CMPR chunk prevents the
following DSD audio chunk from being recognized.

Include the optional padding when skipping a whole DSDIFF chunk. Keep
DSF chunk sizes and the 16-byte FRM8/PROP container entry unchanged.

Reference: https://www.sonicstudio.com/pdf/dsd/DSDIFF_1.5_Spec.pdf
Source: ralph-irving/squeezelite 72e1fd8abfa9b2f8e9636f033247526920878718
Upstream: Not submitted (local correction)

diff --git a/dsd.c b/dsd.c
--- a/dsd.c
+++ b/dsd.c
@@ -187,3 +187,4 @@ static int _read_header(void) {
 		if (!consume) {
-			consume = (s32_t)((d->type == DSDIFF) ? len + 12 : len);
+			// DSDIFF chunk sizes exclude the padding byte after an odd-sized body.
+			consume = (s32_t)((d->type == DSDIFF) ? len + 12 + (len & 1) : len);
 		}
